{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012vSZCkgQdToEhRaXUNEozz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.3-uc001-uniq\n     2→title: \"Filter adjacent duplicate lines via uniq\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go uniq binary on a file or stdin. The binary processes adjacent\n     6→  duplicate lines, printing each unique run once by default, or filtering by duplicate-\n     7→  only or unique-only modes. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go\n     8→  binary and the Homebrew reference binary (guniq from coreutils) with identical inputs\n     9→  and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd028-uniq.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/uniq.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go uniq binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: printf 'a\\na\\nb\\n' | ./bin/uniq\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/uniq reads lines one at a time, comparing each to the previous line (after\n    25→      any field/char skipping and case folding). When a new distinct line is encountered,\n    26→      it flushes the current run (if it meets the output filter) and starts a new run.\n    27→  - id: F3\n    28→    step: |\n    29→      At end of input, cmd/uniq flushes the final run. Each flushed line is prefixed\n    30→      with a count if -c is active.\n    31→  - id: F4\n    32→    step: |\n    33→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/uniq and\n    34→      guniq with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    35→  - id: F5\n    36→    step: |\n    37→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    38→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    39→  - id: F6\n    40→    step: |\n    41→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    42→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    43→\n    44→touchpoints:\n    45→  - T1: \"cmd/uniq — run detection, output filtering, count prefix, field/char skip, case folding (prd028-uniq R1, R2, R3)\"\n    46→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    47→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    48→\n    49→success_criteria:\n    50→  - id: S1\n    51→    criterion: cmd/uniq compiles and ./bin/uniq exists after mage build.\n    52→  - id: S2\n    53→    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; adjacent duplicates suppressed, matching guniq.\n    54→  - id: S3\n    55→    criterion: The differential test for -c passes; each line is prefixed with its run count.\n    56→  - id: S4\n    57→    criterion: The differential test for -d passes; only lines from duplicate runs are output.\n    58→  - id: S5\n    59→    criterion: The differential test for -u passes; only truly unique lines are output.\n    60→  - id: S6\n    61→    criterion: The differential test for -i (case-insensitive) passes.\n    62→  - id: S7\n    63→    criterion: The differential test for -f and -s (field/char skip) passes.\n    64→\n    65→out_of_scope:\n    66→  - uniq does not sort its input; tests use pre-sorted or deliberately ordered input.\n    67→  - The --group flag is not implemented.\n    68→\n    69→test_suite: test-rel05.3\n    70→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80e98de1-9ba5-41b6-9248-92412e595065","uuid":"02493563-5feb-44f8-85af-e9628467aa3f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/357/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.3-uc001-uniq.yaml","content":"id: rel05.3-uc001-uniq\ntitle: \"Filter adjacent duplicate lines via uniq\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go uniq binary on a file or stdin. The binary processes adjacent\n  duplicate lines, printing each unique run once by default, or filtering by duplicate-\n  only or unique-only modes. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go\n  binary and the Homebrew reference binary (guniq from coreutils) with identical inputs\n  and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd028-uniq.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/uniq.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go uniq binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'a\\na\\nb\\n' | ./bin/uniq\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/uniq reads lines one at a time, comparing each to the previous line (after\n      any field/char skipping and case folding). When a new distinct line is encountered,\n      it flushes the current run (if it meets the output filter) and starts a new run.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      At end of input, cmd/uniq flushes the final run. Each flushed line is prefixed\n      with a count if -c is active.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/uniq and\n      guniq with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/uniq — run detection, output filtering, count prefix, field/char skip, case folding (prd028-uniq R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/uniq compiles and ./bin/uniq exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; adjacent duplicates suppressed, matching guniq.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -c passes; each line is prefixed with its run count.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for -d passes; only lines from duplicate runs are output.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -u passes; only truly unique lines are output.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for -i (case-insensitive) passes.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: The differential test for -f and -s (field/char skip) passes.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - uniq does not sort its input; tests use pre-sorted or deliberately ordered input.\n  - The --group flag is not implemented.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.3\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
