{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0136gxRQQYsFpseQ8xn5WJ6K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `-D` flag without an argument fails because Go's `flag` package requires a value for `Func` flags. GNU uniq allows `-D` with no argument (defaulting to \"none\"). The standard `flag` package doesn't support optional flag values well. I need to handle this with manual parsing for `-D`.\n\nLet me switch to manual flag parsing for just the `-D` flag, or handle it in a custom way. Actually, the simplest approach is to do the entire flag parsing manually since Go's `flag` package doesn't support optional values. But that would blow past the line limit. Let me use a different approach — pre-process args to transform bare `-D` into `-D=none`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1040,"cache_read_input_tokens":53844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1040},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80e98de1-9ba5-41b6-9248-92412e595065","uuid":"b0f54f70-cb0a-48e9-8f25-17c1c141da03"}
